    "clause": "Skeletons you control and other Zombies you control get +1/+1 and have deathtouch.",
    "status": "OK",
    "evidence": "Static diff: you_skeleton 2/2 -> 3/3, +DEATHTOUCH; opp_skeleton (on the probe board) unchanged; Death Baron itself 2/2 with no deathtouch ('other'). [this card is dealt lethal damage]: you_skeleton back to 2/2, -DEATHTOUCH. No other Zombie is on the probe battlefield, so pack death_baron_1 adds one: seat 0's Zombie and Skeleton get +1/+1 and deathtouch (1 damage from each destroys a 0/6), the Baron, seat 0's Human and seat 1's Zombie and Skeleton do not (1 damage from each leaves the 0/6 alive). Note for G3: layers.py:700 applies every step of a static Seq to the FIRST step's target selector, so mutants of the deathtouch step's own filter are equivalent (no pack can kill them); the two filters here are identical, so the card plays as printed.",
    "issue": ""
